From f8c9dd3aef264a2715869fdd7ff8c1641ceb3da2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:26:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] daemon: RCS chatbot messages through IMSroha

IMSroha's RichMessageReceived (codes.noa.IMSroha.Rcs): a rich card or
carousel (application/vnd.gsma.botmessage, RCC.07 3.6.10), TTA R9's
extended bot message and open rich card (xbotmessage, openrichcard, R9
7.7.4), or a chatbot text with suggestions, each with its botsuggestion
chip list and the chatbot's service ID. It is stored as an incoming RCS
message with the content type, body, chip list and bot ID in new columns;
its text is a readable summary (R9's header, the titles and descriptions,
the open rich card's texts, the footer), which the conversation list, the
notification and anything that cannot show the card use. A message
nobody here understands says "Unsupported message" and the text fields it
has; never nothing. A new lib/chatbot (RichMessage) reads all of it, for
the daemon and the app alike, from RCC.07's wire form and from R9's
RCSMessage/richcardMessage wrapping.

sendSuggestionResponse: a tapped suggested reply is stored as a sent RCS
message showing its display text, and its RCC.07 response (the reply as
received) goes to the bot through SendSuggestionResponse, in reply to the
card's imdn.Message-ID. A suggested action sends its display text and
postback, and nothing when it has no postback. These never go as SMS: a
failed one is failed (R9 7.7.3.1).

botInfo: the chatbot information of a conversation's bot, kept in a
BotInfo table, fetched with GetBotInfo when it is missing or a day old,
and announced with botInfoChanged; its name titles the notification. A
conversation keyed by a chatbot's SIP URI only ever goes over RCS.

Inert without IMSroha, like 0004-0009.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
